[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One app; views are lenses over one daemon-served dataset

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-SDOC-BOARD-ONE-APP-TWO-VIEWS
TITLE: One app; views are lenses over one daemon-served dataset
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: A view requires its own process, deployment, lifecycle or security boundary, or the view count outgrows a flat switcher.
STATEMENT: >>>
One web app serves every browser reading of the canon. A view is a lens over
the same daemon-served dataset -- it may not fetch from a different source --
selected by a global switcher and recorded in the URL (?view=), with node
selection in the #hash so both survive reload and travel in a link. The chrome
(brand, counts, generation, status, refresh) is global and stable across
views. The first two views are Board, the relation canvas, and Perspective,
the data explorer.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Directed by the operator on 2026-09-01 after running the two spikes side by
side. The shape follows beadboard: views as lenses over one live dataset, the
URL as the source of truth for view state, chrome that does not move when the
view does.
<<<
